WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.730
This is our turf!

3
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:12.210
[CROWD]
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

4
00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:14.180
[CRAFTSMAN B]
Any of those
pirates tries to set foot

5
00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.540
on these grounds tonight,
it'll be the last thing they do!

6
00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.310
The honor of Galley-La
depends on it!

7
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:20.680
Is the back door covered?

8
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.050
Yeah, we got guys coverin'
the entire perimeter

9
00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:26.290
of this place and then some.
Nobody's gettin' in here!

10
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.230
[CRAFTSMAN G]
Come on pirates!
I dare ya! Bring it on!

11
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.550
But...

12
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.420
...they're all huge, and
armed, and angry.

13
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.060
We need to be careful.

14
00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:39.690
Those guys have a
reputation for being able

15
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.190
to handle themselves
when push comes to shove.

16
00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.130
We don't wanna rush in

17
00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.430
and do anything
we're gonna regret later.

18
00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.470
[LUFFY]
Yeah, if we
try to barge in swingin'.

19
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.240
We'll just be
askin' for trouble.

20
00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:53.340
Eh...?

21
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.600
[NAMI]
Right, and we
wouldn't want any trouble.

22
00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.140
Says the guy who charged-in
in broad daylight!

23
00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:03.010
Anyway, don't take your
eyes off of 'em, Chopper.

24
00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.580
We don't want any kind of surprise down
there.

25
00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:07.550
Right.

26
00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.710
[ZORO]
Anything happens,
you let us know.

27
00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:11.300
Okay. You got it.

28
00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:14.350
I think we're gonna have a really long
night ahead of us.

29
00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.790
But if we blow our opportunity,
it's over.

30
00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:21.220
We can't let our guard down,
no matter what happens.

31
00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:24.260
If we wanna know
the truth about Robin.

32
00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:27.130
Then it has to be
tonight, or never.

33
00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:31.100
Yeah. I gotta feeling we'll
be talkin' to her real soon.

34
00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:19.650
[LUFFY]

35
00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:32.220
Kalifa.

36
00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.310
Yes, Mr. Iceburg?

37
00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.900
[ICEBURG]
Not to be rude,
but do you mind stepping out

38
00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.810
of the room for a moment?

39
00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.580
No, of course not.

40
00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:42.280
[ICEBURG]
One more thing.

41
00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:45.310
Fetch Paulie. I need
to have a word with him.

42
00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.000
[KALIFA]
Excuse me, Paulie.

43
00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:51.870
[PAULIE]
Huh?

44
00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:53.340
[KALIFA]
Mr. Iceburg needs to see you.

45
00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.180
I assume it's very important.

46
00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:56.880
He asked for me?

47
00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.090
[KALIFA]
Yes. Specifically.

48
00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.320
I have some things
to take care of

49
00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.890
in my office if
anyone needs me.

50
00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.600
Right.

51
00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:07.830
[KAKU]
Seems like
awfully strange timing

52
00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:10.240
for a one-on-one conversation.

53
00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:11.200
What in blazes could it be about?

54
00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.570
Don't have a clue.

55
00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:15.230
[TILESTONE]
It's his will!

56
00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.800
Well, what're
you doin' out here?

57
00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:20.740
Go on in there and talk to him.

58
00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:22.730
[PAULIE]
Uh... sure.

59
00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:24.970
Don't worry... We can
step away from the door

60
00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:26.010
if you're concerned
about privacy.

61
00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.280
[KAKU]
Good idea.

62
00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:33.320
[TILESTONE]
What the heck

63
00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:36.020
could he wanna talk
about with Paulie?!

64
00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.690
Whatever it is,
it's between them.

65
00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:39.360
We got enough to deal with.

66
00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:41.630
I think we need to stay focused on our
pirate problem.

67
00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.300
Right.

68
00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:44.530
Okay, according to Kalifa,

69
00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:48.040
it's a small group with only
seven people on their crew!

70
00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:49.740
The ones to watch out
for are Straw Hat Luffy.

71
00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:52.510
Pirate hunter Zoro
and Nico Robin.

72
00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:53.820
I wouldn't
underestimate the girl

73
00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:55.820
traveling along with
them or that other guy

74
00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.820
with the long, round nose.

75
00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:01.230
Yeah. There are those
two you just mentioned

76
00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.700
along with two others.
Coo-coo!

77
00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:06.700
It doesn't matter what those pirates are
after.

78
00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:09.840
They set foot on this property tonight,
they're done for.

79
00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:14.810
Every single last one of
them, got it? Coo-coo!

80
00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:16.710
[TILESTONE, LULU, and KAKU]
– Right!
– Right!

81
00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:21.350
Yeah. I understand, sir.

82
00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:22.540
I apologize for putting you

83
00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:25.070
in harm's way like this, Paulie.

84
00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:26.580
But this is a very grave matter

85
00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:29.240
and I trust you
can get it done.

86
00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:31.650
Can I put my faith in you?

87
00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:35.250
I give you my word, sir.
I swear. I won't let you down.

88
00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:39.530
You're a good man.

89
00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:41.730
[PAULIE]
Well s'pose I should get on it.

90
00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:43.270
Thank you.

91
00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:46.440
[door opening]

92
00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.710
[HATTORI]
Coo coo.
He done talking with you?

93
00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:53.810
Yeah. Hey listen guys.

94
00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:57.380
Uh. I gotta head out and
take care of somethin' cool?

95
00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:59.180
No problem, that'll be fine.

96
00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:01.450
The four of us will keep watch over things
here.

97
00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:03.620
Thanks.

98
00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:07.070
Just keep Iceburg safe you guys.

99
00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.580
[ICEBURG'S VOICE]
When you leave here.

100
00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:21.550
Go straight to my office
and move my desk.

101
00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:24.590
I want you to lift up the rug and look
underneath it.

102
00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:26.610
There's a safe hidden there.

103
00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:28.510
Jackpot.

104
00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:32.350
[ICEBURG'S VOICE]
Once you find that,

105
00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:37.420
enter this combination.
First, right to number six.

106
00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:44.600
[TRANSPONDER SNAIL]
Puru-puru. Puru-puru.

107
00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.870
Chuk chuk.

108
00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.580
[MASKED WOMAN]
Are you ready?

109
00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:50.880
[MASKED MAN]
Yes, awaiting your signal.

110
00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.510
[MASKED WOMAN]
It will be very soon now.

111
00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:54.480
At that time, the four
of you are to carry out

112
00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:57.420
your respective missions
with ruthless efficiency.

113
00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.940
[MASKED MAN]
As a loyal
member of CP9, you have my word.

114
00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:02.180
Nico Robin, are you ready?

115
00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:05.280
Yes, I am.

116
00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:13.690
Whoa! Something blew up!

117
00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:14.890
Uh?

118
00:07:16.690 --> 00:07:19.760
Oh no! What
the hell was that?

119
00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:21.060
[CRAFTSMAN H]
Grab water, now!

120
00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:22.820
[CRAFTSMAN I]
We got
a man down over here!

121
00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:24.190
[CRAFTSMAN J]
Make sure
that fire doesn't spread

122
00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:25.600
to the building!

123
00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:27.810
Guys. They're shooting at us!

124
00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:28.760
No man!

125
00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:30.760
I'm pretty sure it was some kind of bomb!

126
00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.100
Someone must have set it then!

127
00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:35.050
[CRAFTSMAN N]
Hurry men!
We gotta put out this fire!

128
00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:36.350
[CRAFTSMAN O]
Someone!
Give me a hand!

129
00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:43.950
[MASKED MAN]
Not too subtle,
but it'll do. Let's move!

130
00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:51.860
[CRAFTSMAN P]
The fire's in the
north corner of the first floor!

131
00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:52.960
Is anyone hurt?

132
00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:55.100
[CRAFTSMAN Q]
There've
been no pirates spotted yet!

133
00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:57.940
Everyone keep your
eyes peeled for intruders!

134
00:07:57.960 --> 00:07:59.300
[CRAFTSMAN R]
Stay at your posts men!

135
00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:03.230
Don't let them get inside!

136
00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:08.100
Sir! Iceburg, are you okay?!

137
00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:10.930
Yeah. Just a bit shocked.

138
00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:11.860
[CRAFTSMAN S]
There they are!

139
00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:12.920
Huh?

140
00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:14.350
[CRAFTSMAN T]
It's that guy
in the costume! Get him!

141
00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:16.390
Those bastards!

142
00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:19.760
RAHH! I'll pound
in their faces!

143
00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:20.390
[LULU]
I got your back!

144
00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:22.120
[KAKU]
Wait! Hold on!

145
00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.800
For Pete's sake.

146
00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:28.160
[HATTORI]
Coo coo.

147
00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:32.170
There he goes! Hurry!

148
00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:33.910
We got this clown!

149
00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:36.740
He's alone. Box him in!

150
00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:38.810
Stop! It's the end of the line!

151
00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.930
[CRAFTSMAN W]
He's headed for the roof!

152
00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:06.370
[CRAFTSMAN AA]
So, ya
thought ya could get away.

153
00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:07.640
Didn't ya, punk?

154
00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:11.040
[CRAFTSMAN AA]
It's gonna take a
lot more than that to get by us.

155
00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:14.910
You made a big mistake when you decided to
mess with Galley-La.

156
00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:18.180
Prepare for the beating of your life!

157
00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:21.420
Cause we're not gonna
show any mercy, scumbag.

158
00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:23.820
[MASKED WOMAN]
You can come
at me with all you've got.

159
00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:27.360
But it still won't be enough.

160
00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:28.420
[CRAFTSMAN II]
Got two over here!

161
00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.690
[CRAFTSMAN UU]
They're
headed for the back door!

162
00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.230
[CRAFTSMAN KI]
Let's try and corner them!

163
00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:37.030
Move, move! After them!

164
00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:39.200
[CRAFTSMAN KU]
Don't let
those bastards get inside!

165
00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:47.280
[MASKED MAN]
You have the
floor plan memorized.

166
00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:49.020
Is that correct?

167
00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:50.110
Yes.

168
00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:57.060
So, they all seem pretty
worked up down there.

169
00:09:57.090 --> 00:10:01.130
Yeah. There is definitely
something going on right now.

170
00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:06.160
Alright, then. When are
we gonna make our move?

171
00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:09.380
Hey, where's Luffy?

172
00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:12.190
Ahhh!

173
00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:15.700
[ZORO and NAMI]
– That idiot! What about the plan?!
– That idiot! What about the plan?!

174
00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:19.770
I thought we weren't
gonna rush into anything!

175
00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.730
[CHOPPER]
Too late.

176
00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:24.790
[CRAFTSMAN KA]
They're going for the back door!

177
00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:26.590
Let's head em off!

178
00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:29.120
[CRAFTSMAN KI]
No matter
what, they can't get inside!

179
00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.760
You got alotta
nerve coming here.

180
00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:39.470
After the crap you
tried to pull last night?

181
00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.800
You're gonna pay for what you did!

182
00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:43.540
Oh yeah, you guys are in

183
00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:46.290
for a world of hurt for
messin' with Mr. Iceburg!

184
00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:47.840
Surrender!

185
00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:51.410
[CRAFTSMAN KO]
Give it up now,

186
00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:53.280
and we might just go easy on ya!

187
00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:54.110
[CRAFTSMAN KO.5]
You're surrounded!

188
00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:55.280
There's nowhere to run!

189
00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:56.940
[CRAFTSMAN SA]
We already
know that it's not just the two

190
00:10:56.980 --> 00:10:58.850
of you guys in your
little pirate gang.

191
00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:00.650
Now where are the others?!

192
00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:11.640
He's pullin' out a weapon!

193
00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:13.980
[CRAFTSMAN SHO]
Shoot 'em!

194
00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:33.470
[CRAFTSMAN SE]
No way! They're gone?!

195
00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:35.130
[CRAFTSMAN SO]
What the hell?

196
00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:36.560
[CRAFTSMAN TA]
Where'd they go?

197
00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:46.770
Hey, are you okay?

198
00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:51.420
Man, that guy's a monster.

199
00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:54.420
He flew. He was
flying through the air.

200
00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:56.520
[CRAFTSMAN TSU]
What the hell?

201
00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:59.620
He can fly?

202
00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:03.490
[MASKED WOMAN]
Idiots.
Do you not know when to give up?

203
00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:06.260
Aaaaaah!

204
00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:09.400
[CRAFTSMAN TO]
He's jumping!

205
00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:10.630
[MASKED WOMAN]
Moon Walk!

206
00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:16.600
What the?! He's really flying!

207
00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:20.970
[MASKED WOMAN]
Thorny Road!

208
00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:33.590
[MASKED WOMAN]
I told you
you were bested, didn't I?

209
00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:35.650
[CRAFTSMAN NA]
Get ready! Here he comes!

210
00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:37.150
[CRAFTSMAN NI]
He's gonna
land in the courtyard!

211
00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:38.720
Don't let him escape!

212
00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:40.390
[CRAFTSMAN NU]
There he goes! Get around him!

213
00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:41.550
We can trap him in there!

214
00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:42.980
[CRAFTSMAN NE]
Yeah!

215
00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:47.580
[PAULIE]
This is it.

216
00:12:48.350 --> 00:12:49.820
[SKULL MASK]
Interesting.

217
00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:51.090
Huh?

218
00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:55.500
[BULL MASK]
All this time it was
literally right under our noses.

219
00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:57.500
Hand it over.

220
00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:03.790
[BULL MASK]
You can't possibly
understand its importance.

221
00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:08.310
Who are you bastards?

222
00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:10.060
Where in the hell did you come from?

223
00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:12.060
[SKULL MASK]
From the shadows.

224
00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:14.910
[BULL MASK]
Yes. From the
darkest corners of existence

225
00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.480
we bring with us
the light of justice.

226
00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:21.820
We are Cipher Pol No. 9, an
undercover intelligence agency.

227
00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:25.190
[PAULIE]
Well, no matter
where you freaks came from.

228
00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:27.090
You sure as hell didn't
get in without running

229
00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:29.120
into the Galley-La craftsmen.

230
00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.600
[BULL MASK]
Perhaps we did.

231
00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:31.500
Huh?

232
00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.910
[BULL MASK]
The details
are all very hazy,

233
00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:36.680
a sea of fists and bodies.

234
00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:40.350
What's important is we're here now.

235
00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:42.950
[PAULIE]
I get it.

236
00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:46.450
This ain't just some assassination plot,
is it?

237
00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:47.520
[BULL MASK]
Very astute.

238
00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:50.360
But then, we never claimed
that it was, now did we.

239
00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:53.400
In any case we need what Iceburg
was trying to keep hidden.

240
00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:56.870
The item you hold in
your trembling hand now.

241
00:13:56.900 --> 00:14:00.570
And since you have been
made aware of its existence.

242
00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:03.770
We need to take
your life, as well.

243
00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:08.010
[BULL MASK]
In trusting you to this task,

244
00:14:08.010 --> 00:14:12.380
Iceburg has signed
your death warrant.

245
00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.440
[CRAFTSMAN NI]
What's
the word? Did you find 'em?

246
00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:16.440
Nu-uh!

247
00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:18.540
There's no sign of
those guys anywhere!

248
00:14:18.570 --> 00:14:19.710
They get inside?

249
00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:21.010
There's men standin' guard

250
00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:22.180
at every single point of entry.

251
00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:23.800
No, there's
no way they got in.

252
00:14:24.560 --> 00:14:25.330
[CRAFTSMAN NE]
Dammit!

253
00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:26.300
Then where the
hell did they go?

254
00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:27.840
[CRAFTSMAN NO]
They couldn't've gotten far.

255
00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:29.540
They've gotta be
hiding somewhere!

256
00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:31.870
Search the perimeter
one more time. Got it?!

257
00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:34.710
[CROWD]
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

258
00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:41.520
Here. He's behind this wall.

259
00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:44.880
[MASKED MAN]
Right. Now give me a push.

260
00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:47.200
Huh...?

261
00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:56.670
Incredible. I had a feeling that
you'd be coming back for me.

262
00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:59.010
But I can't believe my eyes.

263
00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.940
Is this how you came in last night?

264
00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:03.710
How is that even possible?

265
00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:05.880
[MASKED MAN]
It's the
power of the Door-Door Fruit.

266
00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:07.680
Where a normal man sees a wall,

267
00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:09.950
I see a prospective entryway.

268
00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:11.190
No matter how thick it may be,

269
00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:14.180
I simply touch it
and it opens for me.

270
00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:17.700
[gunshot]

271
00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:19.990
Hold on. It's not time yet.

272
00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:22.130
[MASKED MAN]
Relax,
it's not a fatal wound,

273
00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:23.960
he'll still be able to talk.

274
00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:26.660
I'm just giving him a taste of what's to
come.

275
00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:28.870
Like an appetizer of pain.

276
00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:31.500
What's more after that,

277
00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:33.180
I don't think he'll be
running off anywhere

278
00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:35.880
before we get the
signal to finish the job.

279
00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:39.850
Or, perhaps I should say to
serve him the main course.

280
00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:42.420
[ICEBURG]
I see.

281
00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:47.540
So that's how CP9
handles things, huh?

282
00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:49.480
[MASKED MAN]
As a matter of fact.

283
00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:51.710
That is how we do it.

284
00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:57.120
That poor Straw Hat boy.

285
00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:03.190
[ICEBURG]
He had nothing
to do with this, did he?

286
00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:05.870
There's no need to beat yourself up about
it.

287
00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:08.810
After all, you simply told the
truth exactly as you saw it,

288
00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:11.040
and I was indeed
here last night.

289
00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:17.250
That was all part of your plan,
wasn't it?

290
00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:18.730
[MASKED MAN]
Right again.

291
00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:20.330
You're alive for two reasons.

292
00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:21.970
First, so you could
tell your story

293
00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.340
of the failed assassination.

294
00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:25.200
Placing a member of
the Straw Hat crew

295
00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:27.010
at the scene of the crime.

296
00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:29.280
Secondly, we were
trying to ferret out

297
00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:31.680
an important document.

298
00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:34.280
The blueprints of a certain ship.

299
00:16:34.310 --> 00:16:36.750
One that has been
passed down in secret

300
00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:39.340
from shipwright to chosen
apprentice for generations.

301
00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:44.250
We knew that with your
life clearly in danger,

302
00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:46.020
you would pass
that document on

303
00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:48.620
to someone you
trusted to keep it safe.

304
00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:54.860
You made that choice earlier
tonight. Your foreman, Paulie.

305
00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:57.930
Our associates are with him this very
moment.

306
00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:01.100
It's all going as
planned, isn't it.

307
00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:04.900
You must be very damn
proud of yourselves.

308
00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.140
[MASKED MAN]
I want you
to see this to its end.

309
00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:09.710
Of course.

310
00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:11.080
[MASKED MAN]
I'll go deal with the riff-raff

311
00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:13.410
standing guard
outside the door.

312
00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:15.010
When the blueprints are secured,

313
00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:16.910
our associates will contact you.

314
00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:21.380
At that time you will have full
clearance to dispose of Iceburg.

315
00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:23.620
Do so at once.

316
00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:28.730
[MASKED MAN]
Make sure
he dies, without fail.

317
00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:32.400
After that, the only remaining loose end
will be Paulie.

318
00:17:32.430 --> 00:17:36.700
He dies, and the truth of what's happened
here dies with him.

319
00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:39.200
The blame will remain
on the Straw Hats,

320
00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:40.820
I know he doesn't listen to me.

321
00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:49.840
It's crazy, but I thought maybe he'd
listen to his own advice.

322
00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:51.940
We are talking about Luffy.

323
00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:53.910
Hey guys. Do you
think that's Robin?

324
00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:57.180
In the middle of all that
commotion down at Galley-La?

325
00:17:57.210 --> 00:18:00.310
No matter what Luffy decided to
do, we still gotta be careful!

326
00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:01.320
Yeah, I know.

327
00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:03.480
But him rushing in like
that might actually work

328
00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:05.450
in our favor.

329
00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:07.350
If you think about
the way he does things,

330
00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:09.420
is he the kind of guy
that's gonna go in through

331
00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:10.920
the back or side entrance?

332
00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:12.070
Not his style.

333
00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:12.990
No way.

334
00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:15.100
So I'm pretty sure
by now he's made a go

335
00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:16.820
at barging straight
through the front door.

336
00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:18.780
And it's safe to
assume that right now

337
00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:20.450
he's running around
inside like crazy,

338
00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:22.960
because he has no idea where
he's going, doncha think?

339
00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:23.980
Oh yeah!

340
00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:25.320
Sounds like him!

341
00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:27.890
Uh-huh! From the
shipwrights' point of view,

342
00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:30.300
he's the leader of the
group that attacked Iceburg.

343
00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:32.000
So if he made it
in there by now,

344
00:18:32.030 --> 00:18:34.930
all of those guys are gonna
be busy trying to catch him!

345
00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.820
Which would mean the guards
have severely thinned out

346
00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:38.770
at the front door,
or at the very least,

347
00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:40.410
they're completely distracted!

348
00:18:40.460 --> 00:18:42.890
So the safest way in right
now is through the front,

349
00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:45.460
right behind all the
chaos in Luffy's wake!

350
00:18:45.490 --> 00:18:47.260
So when he does it, it's completely
stupid.

351
00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:48.860
But if we do the
exact same thing,

352
00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:50.140
it's actually a
brilliant plan, huh?

353
00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:51.270
Yeah, makes sense!

354
00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:54.140
I say that we
should go for it then!

355
00:18:54.220 --> 00:18:56.060
[NAMI]
The gate is right up ahead!

356
00:18:56.060 --> 00:18:58.420
Okay! Ready?!

357
00:18:58.460 --> 00:18:59.760
It's show time!

358
00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:01.390
Here we, go!

359
00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:18.100
This was a dumb idea!

360
00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:21.030
[LUFFY]
Guh, crap. This sucks!

361
00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:26.200
I wanted to jump right though
the front door like a typhoon.

362
00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:29.210
But I'm totally stuck!

363
00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:38.020
Gotta get out.

364
00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:41.350
Gotta get Robin!

365
00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:59.820
[SHIPWRIGHT A]
Huh?
What the hell's going on?!

366
00:19:59.850 --> 00:20:01.620
[TILESTONE]
RAAAAAHHH!

367
00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:03.420
[SHIPWRIGHT A]
Hey!

368
00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:05.360
We need help on the third floor!

369
00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:07.290
Somebody come to the
president's room, quick!

370
00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:09.730
The guards were wiped out!
I need backup!

371
00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:12.360
What d'you mean,
"wiped out"?!

372
00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:13.710
Tilestone!

373
00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:15.700
Kaku and Lucci should be there!

374
00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:17.600
Well, come see.

375
00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:19.590
What?!

376
00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:30.000
RAHHHH!

377
00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:32.440
What?! No way!

378
00:20:32.470 --> 00:20:33.540
[MASKED MAN]
Still no word.

379
00:20:33.550 --> 00:20:36.980
I'm getting tired of dealing with all
these idiots.

380
00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:38.980
[TILESTONE]
How dare you!

381
00:20:39.020 --> 00:20:42.890
I'll kill you! Bastard!

382
00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:44.790
[MASKED MAN]
You're a
noisy one, aren't you?

383
00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:47.290
If you laid a single
finger on Mr. Iceburg,

384
00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:48.960
I'll tear you limb from limb!

385
00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:51.760
[MASKED MAN]
I'd like to see you try.

386
00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:53.740
Iron Body.

387
00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:58.970
Raaaahh! Raaah!

388
00:21:05.980 --> 00:21:07.420
[SHIPWRIGHT D]
Whoa!

389
00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:09.580
He crushed that giant hammer!

390
00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:11.750
[SHIPWRIGHT D.5]
That's not good!

391
00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:13.460
You!

392
00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:14.340
Get your hands of me!

393
00:21:14.340 --> 00:21:15.430
Get your hands off me!

394
00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:18.200
[MASKED MAN]
Hmph!
Are those muscles just for show?

395
00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:19.900
[thinking]
I can't move my arm!

396
00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:22.100
How is this guy
stronger than me?!

397
00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:43.460
[SHIPWRIGHT A]
He's taken out
three foremen all on his own?

398
00:21:46.690 --> 00:21:48.690
Ahhhh!

399
00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:51.000
[SHIPWRIGHT A]
We'll get
reinforcements downstairs!

400
00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:51.910
[MASKED MAN]
Shave!

401
00:21:51.920 --> 00:21:57.690
[sounds of fighting]

402
00:21:57.750 --> 00:21:58.720
[SHIPWRIGHT X]
We found them!

403
00:21:58.720 --> 00:22:00.130
[SHIPWRIGHT F]
It's Roronoa Zoro!

404
00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:01.960
[SHIPWRIGHT G]
They finally showed up!

405
00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:03.180
[SHIPWRIGHT H]
Don't let them get away!

406
00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:05.240
[SHIPWRIGHT I]
That woman is one of them too!

407
00:22:05.270 --> 00:22:06.370
[SHIPWRIGHT J]
After them!

408
00:22:06.460 --> 00:22:08.500
If Luffy isn't here,
then where is he?!

409
00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:10.780
I don't know, why
are you asking me?!

410
00:22:10.990 --> 00:22:13.090
Aaaaaa!

411
00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:14.520
What now?

412
00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:15.920
Well, they've already found us,

413
00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:17.830
so there's no point
in trying to be sneaky.

414
00:22:17.860 --> 00:22:21.000
The only thing left to do
now is to go on the offensive!

415
00:22:22.500 --> 00:22:24.770
[NAMI]
Wait, what do you
think you're doing?!

416
00:22:24.800 --> 00:22:26.370
[ZORO]
Running circles
around the building

417
00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:27.830
won't do us any good.

418
00:22:27.830 --> 00:22:29.300
If we want to find Robin,

419
00:22:29.310 --> 00:22:31.680
then we're gonna have
to force our way through.

420
00:22:31.730 --> 00:22:33.370
Huh?

421
00:22:33.400 --> 00:22:35.370
Yeah, but those are just shipwrights!

422
00:22:35.400 --> 00:22:36.840
They're not the bad guys!

423
00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:39.720
[ZORO]
Then I'll use
the back of my swords!

424
00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:44.220
[ZORO]
If you want
a fight, you got one!

425
00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:51.020
[NAMI and CHOPPER]
– You can still kill people like that, you know!
– You can still kill people like that, you know!

426
00:23:09.860 --> 00:23:13.630
[ICEBURG]
Mwell, what a surprise.

427
00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:14.780
After all this time,

428
00:23:14.820 --> 00:23:19.760
I never thought we'd be
meeting here, Nico Robin.

429
00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:22.320
[ROBIN]
Am I supposed to know you?

430
00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:23.760
[ICEBURG]
No, last night
was the first time we met.

431
00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:29.740
But for a long time
I've wanted to see you.

432
00:23:29.770 --> 00:23:31.770
I even put your wanted
poster up in my room,

433
00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:33.240
so I'd never forget.

434
00:23:34.840 --> 00:23:36.680
Shall I give you an autograph,
then?

435
00:23:36.710 --> 00:23:38.380
[chuckles]

436
00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:40.980
If you sign it in blood!

437
00:23:42.520 --> 00:23:43.740
You wanted to kill me?

438
00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:49.330
That's right. Before
you destroy the world.

439
00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:51.910
Tell me... Why are you
looking for the Poneglyphs?

440
00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:54.840
You must know the risk.

441
00:23:54.870 --> 00:23:56.470
For as long as
anyone can remember,

442
00:23:56.510 --> 00:23:59.120
the World Government has
made it a serious crime

443
00:23:59.150 --> 00:24:01.120
to research them.

444
00:24:01.180 --> 00:24:04.150
Why is that knowledge so important?

445
00:24:04.260 --> 00:24:07.590
If they're so bad, then why do you know
about them?

446
00:24:07.630 --> 00:24:11.260
Knowing that the Poneglyphs
exist is hardly a crime.

447
00:24:11.260 --> 00:24:12.860
But deciphering
them is another matter

448
00:24:12.900 --> 00:24:17.870
and you're the only person in
the world who's capable of that.

449
00:24:17.900 --> 00:24:19.270
That's why the World Government

450
00:24:19.300 --> 00:24:20.770
put such a large
bounty on your head.

451
00:24:20.800 --> 00:24:24.840
Even though you were only
8 years old at the time.

452
00:24:24.880 --> 00:24:27.140
They fear what
you're capable of.

453
00:24:27.310 --> 00:24:29.780
Because you
alone have the power

454
00:24:29.810 --> 00:24:32.450
to revive the ancient weapons.

455
00:24:34.650 --> 00:24:37.890
So, you already know.

456
00:24:39.820 --> 00:24:42.290
Yes, but I never
would've thought

457
00:24:42.290 --> 00:24:44.830
that CP9 was actually real.

458
00:24:44.860 --> 00:24:46.500
And if that's the
case, that means

459
00:24:46.530 --> 00:24:48.230
you've already
left the Straw Hats

460
00:24:48.300 --> 00:24:50.840
and you're helping the
World Government now.

461
00:24:50.870 --> 00:24:52.410
A strange choice for a woman

462
00:24:52.500 --> 00:24:55.380
whose been on their most
wanted list for 20 years,

463
00:24:55.380 --> 00:24:59.220
but, mwell, I suppose
that's not my concern.

464
00:24:59.250 --> 00:25:00.280
If you decipher the Poneglyphs

465
00:25:00.280 --> 00:25:02.680
and rebuild one of the
weapons it doesn't matter

466
00:25:02.710 --> 00:25:05.480
if the person who uses
it's "good" or "evil."

467
00:25:05.490 --> 00:25:07.720
It's all the same in the end.

468
00:25:07.780 --> 00:25:12.120
A weapon can never be used to bring peace
to this world.

469
00:25:12.200 --> 00:25:16.370
All it can bring is destruction.

470
00:25:16.400 --> 00:25:20.670
We've buried the evils of
the past, now let them lie.

471
00:25:23.610 --> 00:25:25.940
You may be right
and I don't disagree.

472
00:25:25.980 --> 00:25:28.580
But you don't know why I'm doing this.

473
00:25:28.610 --> 00:25:31.320
You have no right to tell
me what I'm allowed to do

474
00:25:31.350 --> 00:25:32.880
or not do with my research

475
00:25:32.920 --> 00:25:35.550
or what knowledge
I can or cannot learn.

476
00:25:37.450 --> 00:25:40.680
Mwell, I see what you mean.

477
00:25:40.720 --> 00:25:44.990
But the truth is we might have
more in common than you think.

478
00:25:45.020 --> 00:25:47.260
Perhaps you didn't know.

479
00:25:47.290 --> 00:25:48.420
But I possess the blueprints

480
00:25:48.460 --> 00:25:50.960
for the ancient
weapon known as Pluton.

481
00:25:51.590 --> 00:25:53.600
[ROBIN]
Then they still exist?

482
00:25:53.630 --> 00:25:55.660
[ICEBURG]
Pluton is the
name of a battleship built

483
00:25:55.700 --> 00:25:58.670
on this island many
years in the past.

484
00:26:00.400 --> 00:26:01.840
The shipwrights who
created the weapon

485
00:26:01.870 --> 00:26:05.040
passed on the blueprints as
a sort of insurance policy.

486
00:26:05.040 --> 00:26:07.510
They feared that another
battleship of equal power

487
00:26:07.540 --> 00:26:10.850
would be necessary if Pluton
ever fell into the wrong hands.

488
00:26:10.960 --> 00:26:12.430
Thankfully, the ship was lost

489
00:26:12.490 --> 00:26:15.100
to history before
that could happen.

490
00:26:15.130 --> 00:26:18.370
And now the government
wants to revive that power,

491
00:26:18.400 --> 00:26:21.900
when there's no force
strong enough to oppose it.

492
00:26:22.170 --> 00:26:23.940
A part of me hopes that
you didn't know that

493
00:26:23.940 --> 00:26:25.910
when you agreed
to help them out

494
00:26:25.940 --> 00:26:27.930
but that doesn't
really matter now.

495
00:26:27.930 --> 00:26:31.340
A man named Tom entrusted those blueprints
to me.

496
00:26:31.370 --> 00:26:33.000
And he also told me
about a young girl

497
00:26:33.040 --> 00:26:37.580
who was the sole survivor of
the Ohara incident 20 years ago.

498
00:26:37.610 --> 00:26:39.980
He said despite her age,
she was still dangerous,

499
00:26:40.010 --> 00:26:41.850
because she had
the same ideology

500
00:26:41.880 --> 00:26:43.580
as the devils from Ohara.

501
00:26:43.620 --> 00:26:45.680
In honor of Tom and
the other shipwrights,

502
00:26:45.700 --> 00:26:48.600
it's my responsibility
to stop you!

503
00:26:48.640 --> 00:26:50.040
Of course, now that
the government knows

504
00:26:50.090 --> 00:26:53.330
that the blueprints exist the
logical solution would be

505
00:26:53.360 --> 00:26:55.460
to burn them and
be done with this mess.

506
00:26:55.490 --> 00:26:58.060
But I can't do that because
as long as you're alive,

507
00:26:58.100 --> 00:27:00.900
there's a chance that the
weapon could be rebuilt!

508
00:27:14.500 --> 00:27:17.520
[ROBIN]
Is that all you
want to say before you die?

509
00:27:17.850 --> 00:27:19.820
Oh, and with all due respect,

510
00:27:19.850 --> 00:27:22.990
even if you had killed me,
nothing would've changed.

511
00:27:23.020 --> 00:27:25.960
The government doesn't need me
to steal the blueprints from you

512
00:27:25.990 --> 00:27:28.630
and I'm sure they've already
accomplished that anyway.

513
00:27:36.110 --> 00:27:40.780
Mwell, let's not get
ahead of ourselves here.

514
00:27:41.780 --> 00:27:44.270
You're the ones who've fallen for my trap.

515
00:27:55.770 --> 00:27:56.470
Oh!

516
00:27:56.470 --> 00:27:58.240
That's it!

517
00:28:03.930 --> 00:28:05.460
I thought I'd never get out of there!

518
00:28:07.280 --> 00:28:09.020
Man, that was terrible!

519
00:28:09.050 --> 00:28:11.350
Okay. Let's get
it right this time!

520
00:28:11.410 --> 00:28:13.250
I'll find Robin for sure!

521
00:28:13.280 --> 00:28:21.060
Gum-Gum Rocket!

522
00:28:37.590 --> 00:28:40.390
[BULL MASK]
I'm afraid you're
no match for our martial arts.

523
00:28:43.880 --> 00:28:46.920
[BULL MASK]
Now stop resisting
and hand us the document

524
00:28:47.430 --> 00:28:49.790
before you soil
it with your blood.

525
00:28:52.150 --> 00:28:53.710
[thinking]
Damn it...

526
00:28:54.630 --> 00:28:57.670
I really thought
I could beat them...

527
00:29:06.440 --> 00:29:08.970
[PAULIE]
I shoulda known better.

528
00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:10.970
This was all my idea.

529
00:29:11.010 --> 00:29:13.740
Iceburg didn't
tell me to fight.

530
00:29:13.840 --> 00:29:17.850
He told me to get the hell out of here.

531
00:29:17.950 --> 00:29:21.480
To run and leave the blueprints behind.

532
00:29:24.130 --> 00:29:27.070
[PAULIE]
Ya know why?

533
00:29:27.090 --> 00:29:29.430
'Cause those are
nothing but fakes.

534
00:29:29.460 --> 00:29:30.490
[SKULL MASK]
Wha...?

535
00:29:30.540 --> 00:29:31.600
[BULL MASK]
What?

536
00:29:31.650 --> 00:29:33.320
[SKULL MASK]
He can't be serious.

537
00:29:33.350 --> 00:29:36.060
[BULL MASK]
What a waste of time.

538
00:29:36.140 --> 00:29:37.510
[PAULIE]
I don't know who you are,

539
00:29:37.540 --> 00:29:40.650
but this means your
plan's a bust, huh?

540
00:29:40.650 --> 00:29:44.520
Too bad. Sucks to be you.

541
00:29:44.550 --> 00:29:47.050
Funny thing is
I don't even know

542
00:29:47.090 --> 00:29:50.560
what you bastards were
looking for in the first place.

543
00:29:50.590 --> 00:29:54.130
If you think you've outwitted CP9,
you're wrong.

544
00:29:54.160 --> 00:29:56.400
You're merely delaying the inevitable.

545
00:29:57.530 --> 00:30:00.430
[BULL MASK]
At any rate, even
though you're only a decoy.

546
00:30:00.450 --> 00:30:04.280
Now that you know the truth,
we can't let you live.

547
00:30:10.640 --> 00:30:13.180
[loud crash]

548
00:30:17.550 --> 00:30:19.950
Damn it! I got stuck again!

549
00:30:20.060 --> 00:30:22.000
Stupid walls getting
in my way all the time!

550
00:30:22.030 --> 00:30:23.570
I hate 'em, I hate 'em!

551
00:30:24.180 --> 00:30:25.470
What? Straw Hat.

552
00:30:26.370 --> 00:30:28.300
Hey, it's the rope guy!

553
00:30:28.340 --> 00:30:30.310
What's going on in here?

554
00:30:30.340 --> 00:30:33.340
Whoa, are you okay?
You're covered in blood!

555
00:30:33.380 --> 00:30:35.140
You sure did surprise me!

556
00:30:35.180 --> 00:30:36.980
[PAULIE]
Look who's talking!

557
00:30:37.010 --> 00:30:39.350
At least I'm not crashing through walls.

558
00:30:39.480 --> 00:30:41.150
[BULL MASK]
Straw Hat Luffy.

559
00:30:41.260 --> 00:30:44.400
How kind of you to come here
to take blame for the crime.

560
00:30:44.430 --> 00:30:48.230
Oh! I get it! You guys in
the masks must be the ones

561
00:30:48.270 --> 00:30:51.100
that're forcing Robin to
do all this bad stuff, huh?!

562
00:30:51.140 --> 00:30:53.670
You give her back, you bastards!

563
00:30:53.700 --> 00:30:57.130
If I wasn't stuck right now, you'd be in
big trouble!

564
00:30:57.130 --> 00:30:58.340
[SKULL MASK]
Tempest Kick.

565
00:30:58.370 --> 00:30:59.670
Uhn?

566
00:31:12.420 --> 00:31:16.320
He cut right through the wall!

567
00:31:16.350 --> 00:31:18.320
Hey, behind you!

568
00:31:29.440 --> 00:31:31.030
What are these...?

569
00:31:32.250 --> 00:31:34.350
[BULL MASK]
This is an emergency situation.

570
00:31:34.350 --> 00:31:36.330
We don't have time to deal with you.

571
00:31:36.330 --> 00:31:37.550
I can't move!

572
00:31:37.560 --> 00:31:39.330
[BULL MASK]
Restrain Paulie too.

573
00:31:39.360 --> 00:31:41.330
He's given us enough
trouble already.

574
00:31:41.420 --> 00:31:42.520
[SKULL MASK]
Right.

575
00:31:46.190 --> 00:31:50.260
[PAULIE]
Hggh... Hgggh... Haaaaaaah!

576
00:31:51.740 --> 00:31:57.250
[TRANSPONDER SNAIL]
Puru-puru. Puru-puru.

577
00:31:57.270 --> 00:31:58.340
Click.

578
00:31:58.380 --> 00:32:00.740
[BULL MASK]
It's me.
We've hit a snag in the plan.

579
00:32:01.350 --> 00:32:03.750
Everyone head to the bedroom immediately.

580
00:32:03.750 --> 00:32:05.570
Don't shoot Iceburg yet.

581
00:32:06.200 --> 00:32:10.170
You understand?
I absolutely need him alive.

582
00:32:14.070 --> 00:32:15.180
[MASKED WOMAN]
This has been a delight,

583
00:32:15.210 --> 00:32:17.040
but I'm afraid our time is up.

584
00:32:17.080 --> 00:32:18.310
Hmm?

585
00:32:18.340 --> 00:32:20.240
[MASKED WOMAN]
You see, I have
a pressing matter to attend to.

586
00:32:20.250 --> 00:32:22.020
Running away, are you?

587
00:32:22.030 --> 00:32:23.130
[MASKED WOMAN]
Not at all.

588
00:32:30.150 --> 00:32:31.420
[MASKED WOMAN]
I'm just
finishing you quickly,

589
00:32:31.450 --> 00:32:32.650
that's all.

590
00:32:33.620 --> 00:32:34.590
[SHIPWRIGHT J]
Lulu!

591
00:32:34.660 --> 00:32:35.960
Come back!

592
00:32:39.390 --> 00:32:40.930
[SHIPWRIGHT K]
She's flying again!

593
00:32:42.400 --> 00:32:45.670
[PAULIE]
Hey, you all right?

594
00:32:46.760 --> 00:32:49.400
[LUFFY]
You kidding? This is nothing.

595
00:32:49.440 --> 00:32:51.310
[PAULIE]
That's good, I guess.

596
00:32:51.340 --> 00:32:53.680
But why did you come
here in the first place?

597
00:32:53.760 --> 00:32:57.360
Everyone still thinks you're
the ones who attacked Iceburg.

598
00:32:57.390 --> 00:32:59.500
Sorry about that, by the way.

599
00:32:59.530 --> 00:33:01.670
I realize I mighta
jumped the gun a little.

600
00:33:01.700 --> 00:33:05.140
[LUFFY]
No big deal.
We are pirates, after all.

601
00:33:05.170 --> 00:33:06.570
Anyway, the point
is those weird guys

602
00:33:06.600 --> 00:33:09.710
in the masks took
one of our crew.

603
00:33:09.960 --> 00:33:11.590
So we're here to get her back.

604
00:33:13.340 --> 00:33:15.100
Nico Robin.

605
00:33:19.970 --> 00:33:22.440
So, you're good at fighting, aren't you?

606
00:33:22.470 --> 00:33:24.070
Hell yeah!

607
00:33:24.100 --> 00:33:26.040
Then you can beat those guys, huh?

608
00:33:26.080 --> 00:33:29.150
You bet.

609
00:33:29.300 --> 00:33:30.470
Good.

610
00:33:30.500 --> 00:33:33.070
We can do this thing together.
'Cause I'm ready to fight!

611
00:33:33.100 --> 00:33:33.800
Oh yeah?

612
00:33:33.800 --> 00:33:34.970
Of course I am!

613
00:33:34.980 --> 00:33:36.650
I mean you think
I'm just gonna let

614
00:33:36.710 --> 00:33:38.140
some weirdoes
waltz in outta nowhere,

615
00:33:38.180 --> 00:33:40.750
kick my ass and
then kill Iceburg?!

616
00:33:40.780 --> 00:33:42.020
Not a chance!

617
00:33:42.040 --> 00:33:44.010
Who do those punks,
think they are, anyway?!

618
00:33:44.020 --> 00:33:46.620
To hell with all this secret agent crap!

619
00:33:49.160 --> 00:33:50.860
Iceburg is...

620
00:33:51.990 --> 00:33:54.100
...more than just my boss.

621
00:33:54.130 --> 00:33:56.630
He's my teacher.
He made me a shipwright.

622
00:33:56.660 --> 00:33:58.500
I can't let him die.

623
00:33:58.530 --> 00:33:59.970
But look at you, you're a mess.

624
00:33:59.980 --> 00:34:02.050
I told you, I'm ready
to fight those bastards,

625
00:34:02.090 --> 00:34:03.290
and I'm not giving up!

626
00:34:03.290 --> 00:34:07.460
I don't care what happens to me
as long as I can save Iceburg!

627
00:34:07.490 --> 00:34:08.960
Auugh!

628
00:34:08.990 --> 00:34:09.890
But I can't even move,

629
00:34:09.920 --> 00:34:14.790
cause I'm stuck to
the floor! This sucks!

630
00:34:14.820 --> 00:34:20.090
Yeah! I know! This sucks!
Auuugh!

631
00:34:20.120 --> 00:34:22.430
Auuugh!

632
00:34:22.430 --> 00:34:24.330
Auugh!

633
00:34:42.620 --> 00:34:48.050
Go home! I have nothing
to give you people!

634
00:34:48.090 --> 00:34:50.420
[BULL MASK]
Then we have
a problem, don't we?

635
00:34:57.460 --> 00:35:00.760
[BULL MASK]
What does one say to
a man who's marked for death?

636
00:35:03.030 --> 00:35:05.530
First, let me be frank.

637
00:35:05.540 --> 00:35:08.090
You disappoint me.

638
00:35:12.600 --> 00:35:14.300
[ICEBURG]
Lucci!

639
00:35:14.580 --> 00:35:16.140
[SKULL MASK]
This is your own fault.

640
00:35:17.040 --> 00:35:18.740
You should've handed
over the blueprints

641
00:35:21.440 --> 00:35:23.570
when the government
asked nicely.

642
00:35:24.440 --> 00:35:26.020
[ICEBURG]
Kaku!

643
00:35:26.540 --> 00:35:29.080
Pity. I was hoping
we could walk away

644
00:35:29.110 --> 00:35:33.380
from this story without
resorting to violence.

645
00:35:33.410 --> 00:35:34.850
[ICEBURG]
Kalifa.

646
00:35:34.880 --> 00:35:38.090
It's a shame you're as hard-headed as your
master.

647
00:35:38.120 --> 00:35:40.960
[ICEBURG]
Blueno, from the bar.

648
00:35:41.080 --> 00:35:46.590
That means you've been with
the government all this time.

649
00:35:46.650 --> 00:35:47.720
Indeed.

650
00:35:47.500 --> 00:35:52.380
<b>The World Government's Covert Intelligence Service
Cipher Pol No. 9</b>

651
00:35:47.750 --> 00:35:48.760
Needless to say,

652
00:35:48.790 --> 00:35:52.730
going undercover was
like second-nature to us.

653
00:35:52.760 --> 00:35:55.530
Now since everyone's
being so honest

654
00:35:55.560 --> 00:35:59.130
with each other,
let's try this again.

655
00:35:59.170 --> 00:36:01.770
I don't have time to play games.

656
00:36:01.800 --> 00:36:07.070
Tell me before someone
else gets hurt. Where is it?

657
00:36:07.110 --> 00:36:11.010
Where are the blueprints for the ancient
weapon Pluton?
